<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Harmony Q1 pre-capex net profit falls.</title>
<headline>Harmony Q1 pre-capex net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital spending  39.59  vs 56.51</p>
<p>    Capital spending			   7.51  vs 11.51</p>
<p>Gold output (kg)</p>
<p>    - underground			     5,479  vs 5,282</p>
<p>    - surface				     150  vs 145</p>
<p>Tonnes milled/treated</p>
<p>    - underground			  1,355,000 vs 1,333,000</p>
<p>    - surface				  405,000 vs   384,000</p>
<p>Yield (gram/t)</p>
<p>    - underground				 4,04 vs 3.96</p>
<p>    - surface				     0.37 vs 0.38</p>
<p>Cash operating cost (rand/kg)	     45.040 vs 44.272</p>
<p>Revenue (rand/kg)			     51.668 vs 56.151</p>
<p>Full name: Harmony Gold Mining Ltd, managed by Randgold and Exploration Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Underground gold production included an estimated 166 kilograms of gold from the final clean-up of the St Helena plant which previously treated ore from Unisel.</p>
<p>A major contributing factor to the increase in cash operating costs was an increase of eight percent in stores expenditure resulting from an increase in production as well as an increase in maintenance of machinery and equipment.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
